cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, methodology, or published search records, please cite it using this metadata."
type: software
title: "SETIsearch: Panchromatic (>4-Octave, 0.1145-2.515 um) Space-FUV, Optical, Near-IR Echelle Laser, Frequency-Comb, Radio & Photometric Technosignature Pipeline"
abstract: >-
  Prospectively locked, reproducible archival searches and pure-stdlib numerical audits
  for panchromatic space far-UV (HST_STIS E140M, 0.1145-0.1710 um), near-UV (VLT UVES_NUV),
  optical (HARPS, HARPS-N, ESPRESSO HR/UHR, OHP SOPHIE, OHP ELODIE, CFHT ESPaDOnS), far-red
  (VLT UVES_RED, CARMENES_VIS), near-infrared YJH (NIRPS_HE), thermal K-band (VLT CRIRES+),
  and simultaneous YJHK (CFHT SPIRou APERO 0.7.295) laser and periodic frequency-comb
  technosignatures (0.1145-2.515 um, 4.457 octaves across 12 spectrographs / 13 arms plus
  FEROS; 220 unique stars and 1,567 high-resolution echelle exposures totaling 365.80 h in
  V3.0-V3.9 + COMB_V4_1 with Keplerian planetary de-Doppler, G4_V38 Fiber-B simultaneous-cal
  bleed veto [577->0], 2D CCD/MAMA/H2RG/H4RG vetoes, sparse G6 coincidence gating, and
  uniform all-sky COMB_V4_1 matched filtering across 100% of D079-D088), unified with
  planetary-rest-frame 1.4 GHz narrowband radio searches (Parkes/GBT) and TESS specular
  light-sail photometry achieving 23/23 (100%) radio-echelle closure across a 220-system
  multi-messenger synthesis (0 verified ETI detections, 0.0973 W FUV limit on Proxima Cen).
